===Etymology===
From {{inh|sq|sqj-pro|*widertjā}}, with loss of the first unstressed syllable, from {{inh|sq|ine-pro|*sweyd-}} (compare {{cog|grc|ἱδρώς}}, {{cog|en|sweat}}, {{cog|it|sudore}}).<ref>{{R:sq:Orel|page=69}}</ref> For Albanian ''d'' < PIE ''*sw'' compare {{m|sq|diell}}.

Alternatively, from {{inh|sq|sqj-pro|*dértsā||t=effusion}}, with no further general accepted reconstruction. Ultimately from {{inh|sq|ine-pro|*dʰérǵʰ-ti̯(-)ah₂}} (or *dʰérǵʰ-ii̯o-n ?), with a semantic shift from "revolution" to "(sweat) effusion". Neri considers an etymological connection to {{inh|sq|ine-pro|*sweyd-}}, and relation to Greek {{l|grc|ῑ̆̔δρώς}} and Latin {{l|la|sūdor}}, problematic, specifically with the reconstruction of *su̯idroti̯ah₂, because of the phonetic law postulated by Pederson #sw > Alb. #d, which is contradicted by several counterexamples, such as {{l|sq|vjehërr}} (compare also {{l|sq|vëlla}}). While the above etymology suggests a comparison to {{l|sq|diell}} for #sw > #d, the etymology of diell is also contested. Another problem is an unexpected simplification of *dr > *d.<ref>{{R:sq:DPEWA|14011}}</ref>

